# Angular

## Structure
- `src/app/core/`: singletons (auth, http interceptors, guards, api client). Imported only by the app shell/routes.
- `src/app/shared/`: reusable presentational components, pipes, directives. No feature imports.
- `src/app/features/<feature>/`: lazy-loaded routes, `pages/` (smart) and `components/` (presentational).

## Components
- Standalone only, `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`.
- `inject()` over constructor params; `input()` / `output()` / `model()` signal APIs.
- Built-in control flow (`@if`, `@for` with `track`, `@switch`). No `*ngIf`/`*ngFor`.
- Presentational components: inputs in, outputs out, no services. Smart pages own data fetching.
- No logic in templates beyond simple expressions; derive with `computed()`.

## State & data
- Feature state in an injectable service exposing readonly signals (`asReadonly()`), mutating via methods.
- HTTP lives in `*-api.service.ts` returning typed observables/`resource`; convert with `toSignal` at the edge.
- Use shared types from `@workflow/shared`; never redeclare API DTOs.
- Unsubscribe automatically (`takeUntilDestroyed`, `toSignal`); no manual subscription bookkeeping.

## Forms
- Typed reactive forms (`FormBuilder.nonNullable`), validators mirror the shared Zod rules.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
@Component({ selector: 'app-zap-card', changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush, template: `...` })
export class ZapCardComponent {
  readonly zap = input.required<Zap>();
  readonly toggled = output<boolean>();
}
```

## Style
- SCSS per component, design tokens via CSS variables; no inline styles. Accessible labels on every control.
